WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.612
How many of you have been 
bothered by mosquitoes

00:00:01.612 --> 00:00:03.475
when you're outside, enjoying the barbecue

00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:05.356
or visiting the local wetlands during summer?

00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:07.957
What about that mosquito that buzzes 
around your bedroom at night?

00:00:07.957 --> 00:00:09.571
I'm going to leave you&nbsp;with three tips

00:00:09.571 --> 00:00:11.933
that can help you stop 
the bite of mosquitoes

00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.443
and the buzz of 
mosquitoes this&nbsp;summer.

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:16.497
First of all, don't create opportunities 
for mosquitoes in your backyard.

00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:19.761
Anything that&nbsp;traps water after rainfall 
will be a source of mosquitoes,

00:00:19.761 --> 00:00:24.893
so tip out, cover up or remove these&nbsp;
water-holding containers in your backyard.

00:00:24.893 --> 00:00:26.559
Clean your gutters and your drains,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:30.052
reduce that standing&nbsp;water that mosquitoes 
love so much around our homes.

00:00:30.052 --> 00:00:34.069
Secondly, insect repellents are a safe and&nbsp;
effective way to avoid mosquito bites.

00:00:34.069 --> 00:00:36.607
Make sure you apply it as a nice, even coat

00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:38.734
over all exposed&nbsp;areas of skin.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.379
Unless you've got complete cover,

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:42.085
those mosquitoes will find a way

00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:44.190
to find that&nbsp;gap in your repellent and bite.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.217
Lastly, we know that operating
 a fan in a bedroom

00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:49.554
can help reduce&nbsp;those mosquitoes that
 come in and buzz around our ears at night.

00:00:49.554 --> 00:00:52.968
It disperses the smells and the&nbsp;temperatures
around that body that attracts them;

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:56.520
it might make it a bit harder for that&nbsp;
mossie to fly around and find us as well.

